A||N||3||Sooner||Tack running backward & stall at idle||||5||
Z||000000||Sooner||11-12-2001||04:49 AM||||I have a 86 2.8 V6 automatic with 103K that I recently purchased. It is doing 2 things that have me baffled:<P>1. Tach reads normally from 0-1500 rpm then runs backwards. Specifically, it appears to work normally between 0-1500 rpm, then when you accelerate past that point it literally runs backwards. Doesn't jump or anything, just runs backwards.<P>2. The engine stalls at idle. When I come to a stop, whether cold or warm, the rpms will drop so low that the engine stalls and dies.<P>Don't know if the two are connected, but I can't figure it out. Computer pulls a 33 code for the MAP. I have checked MAP vaccum lines & replaced the MAP. I have replaced plugs, wires, rotor, cap, IAC. Coil & alternator were also recently replaced. Any ideas?<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroJoe||11-12-2001||01:08 PM||||Tach problem sounds like the tach filter, which is a small round can with two wires going into it near the ignition coil.  When they go bad, which they usually do, the tach starts to do all sorts of crazy things.  Rodney Dickman sells replacements.  <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rodneydickman.com</A> <P>As for the stalling, did you also replace your fuel filter?  Try that, possibly you arent getting sufficient fuel pressure to keep an idle.  Also, check and make sure that your timing is also correct.||||reg||1
Z||000002||avengador1||11-12-2001||02:16 PM||||As for your stalling, it could also be that the torque converter is staying engaded.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Sooner||11-12-2001||02:19 PM||||I had wondered about the tach filter (have been reading other posts), but it did not appear to be what others had described. However, I'll do some checking.<P>I replaced fuel filter. Ran the same before as after. I'll check into timing. That may be the simplest thing that I didn't think to check. . .   ||||reg||3
